<title>UK: Ghana cocoa purchases behind year earlier season.</title>
<headline>Ghana cocoa purchases behind year earlier season.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ghana cocoa purchases to the end of the 16th week of the 1996/97 season were a cumulative 272,871 tonnes compared with 312,142 tonnes at the end of the 17th week of the year-earlier season.</p>
<p>The Ghana Cocoa Board said it purchased 12,365 tonnes of cocoa in the 16th week ended January 30, 1997 compared with 8,275 tonnes in the 17th week ended February 1, 1996 of the year-earlier season.</p>
<p>The board bought 7,803 tonnes of cocoa for the 16th week ended January 25 last year of the year-earlier season, bringing the cumulative purchases to 303,867 tonnes.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4985</p>
